#
# Counter-example for the `math:` expression lowering
# (crates/logic/src/physical/lower.rs, MathLoweringError::NumberLiteralMissingValue): a
# math:NumberLiteral root with no math:literalValue at all. The lowering dispatches
# ex:root as a NumberLiteral leaf and demands exactly one math:literalValue to carry as
# the leaf's value; finding none is a HARD FAIL distinct from the (unrelated)
# StringOnlyComputableExpression source-lint rule. The authored math:structuralKey lets
# the reasoned-graph gate (crates/logic/src/math_expression.rs,
# check_structural_key_on_rejected_expression) also reach this fixture, so it registers
# on the native rust-validator channel alongside driving the in-crate variant-liveness
# test directly against the real production lowering entry point.
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:root a math:NumberLiteral ;
    math:structuralKey "not-a-real-digest" .
